=== Public FMT / app-header layouts (evidence) ===

A) Classic samsung-ipc / Replicant / osmocom Wireshark FMT
   Source: libsamsung-ipc include/radio.h (morphis); Wireshark-dev
           202202/msg00028 (GNUtoo packet-samsung-ipc); Replicant
           SamsungIpcDissector wiki.
   struct ipc_header / ipc_fmt_header (packed 7B):
     u16 length;  /* total incl. header */
     u8  mseq;
     u8  aseq;
     u8  group;   /* command high */
     u8  index;   /* command low  */
     u8  type;    /* REQ: EXEC=1 GET=2 SET=3 CFRM=4 EVENT=5
                    RSP: INDI=1 RESP=2 NOTI=3 */
   command = (group<<8)|index
   SEC bank (include/sec.h): IPC_SEC_SIM_STATUS=0x0501, ...
     NO SIM_INIT_REQ; NO 0x2f50 / 0x2f52 in public SEC table.
   Closest hypothetical map of catalog msgid onto this header:
     group=0x2f index=0x50  => command word 0x2f50
     length = 7 + body_hint(=2) = 9
     type = ? (EXEC/GET/SET unproven for Shannon OEM catalog)
     mseq/aseq = ?
     body[2] = ? (zeros unproven)
   Verdict: STRUCT known publicly; BINDING to Shannon OEM catalog
            msgid 0x2f50 NOT evidenced (SEC group is 0x05, not 0x2f).

B) Soft SIT FMT on Pixel umts_ipc0 (our factory / live)
   App 12B: type:u8 pad:u8 id:u16le len:u16le token:u32le [body]
   Evidenced: GetSimStatus id=0x0200 len=12; VerifyPin id=0x0201
   Twin check: soft 0x0201 body != OEM catalog 0x2f52 body_hint=10
   No SIT dual 0x0200<->0x2f50 / 0x0201<->0x2f52 in MAIN.
   Verdict: NOT the OEM catalog wire dialect.

C) Kernel EXYNOS 12B wrap (CPIF / sipc5 link_header)
   Public kernel: exynos_build_header (modem_v1 / modem_if families)
   Live kprobe (SitOem Ping on oem_ipc0):
     sync=0xABCD | frame_seq | frag_cfg=0xC000 | len=12+count
     | ch=0x81 | pad | <userspace app bytes passthrough>
   Userspace write = app only; NO msgid in EXYNOS header.
   Verdict: outer transport ONLY; does not supply catalog app hdr.

D) SitOem protobuf on oem_ipc0
   Live Ping REQUEST/RESPONSE proven; schema exhaust: no SIM/INIT.
   Verdict: different dialect from catalog 0x2f50.

E) Comsecuris / Hardwear.io / ShannonBaseband
   Document SHM FMT/RAW rings + internal qitem_header (src/dst/msg).
   Do NOT publish Shannon OEM catalog app header or 0x2f50 body.

F) AOSP / Google sepolicy
   /dev/oem_ipc[0-7] labeled radio_device -- node existence only;
   no app-header layout comments for catalog SIM_INIT.

=== MAIN catalog stride-28 cross-check ===
  @0x6de740 SIM_INIT_REQ:     body_hint=2  msgid=0x2f50 meta=0x10104
                              rsp=0  +0x18=4 (class tag, not token len)
  @0x6de874 SIM_VERIFYPIN_REQ: body_hint=10 msgid=0x2f52 meta=0x10104
                              rsp=0x2fa1 +0x18=0
  meta 0x10104 common across SIM REQ bank -- opaque; NOT proven as
  classic sipc type / SIT type / EXYNOS frag_cfg.

=== Map attempt: 0x2f50 onto public headers ===
  - classic 7B sipc_fmt: closest=group/index=0x2f/0x50; gap=mseq,aseq,type,body[2]
  - soft SIT 12B: closest=would put id=0x2f50; gap=SIT dialect; twin sizes contradict
  - EXYNOS 12B: closest=kernel only; gap=no msgid; app still missing
  - SitOem protobuf: closest=n/a; gap=no SIM_INIT in schema
  - catalog meta alone: closest=body_hint=2; gap=body CONTENTS unknown

